 Remove context :
 ----------------
 In SAP CPI especially when working with XML payloads, message mappings often deal with multiple levels of context.
 The removeContext() function is used within a message mapping to flatten the structure  by removing context levels.

 Purpose:
 The removeContext function removes all context changes and brings an values to the same level , making them part of
 the same context.


 When to Use:
 In SAP CPI every node in a mapping may create its own context. This impacts how loops and conditions behave. by removing context
 ->  you make the data more linear
 -> it becomes easier to process in functions like useOneASMany or custom logic.



before remove context
Context 1: [Apple]
Context 2: [Orange]
Context 3: [Banana]

after remove context
[Apple, Orange, Banana]

Only the context breaks are removed, but all values remain.



